{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good evening, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , one of the hospitalists. I understand you came in with chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, doctor. I had two episodes this week. The first lasted about an hour when I was trying to get comfortable in bed. It was a squeezing pain across my chest, and I felt short of breath and numbness in both arms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And did you take anything for it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I took my nitroglycerin under the tongue, and it went away. I thought maybe it was my mattress, so I bought a new one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good you took the nitro. But then you had another episode?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the next night around 9:30. Same kind of pain, lasted about 90 minutes. I just lay still and it eventually went away. I didn’t have any fever or cough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. You’ve had heart issues before, correct? I see you’ve had stents placed in your right coronary artery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, a few months ago. They did a procedure with rotational atherectomy and put in two stents. I’ve been on aspirin and Plavix since then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right. And your dialysis — you’re on hemodialysis three times a week?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, Mondays, Wednesdays, Fridays. My access is in my left arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We’ve done some tests. Your EKG shows sinus bradycardia, but no acute changes. Your troponin was slightly elevated at 0.04, but it’s been stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a heart attack?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. In someone with kidney disease, troponin can be a bit higher normally. But the pattern and your symptoms suggest unstable angina — chest pain from reduced blood flow, not a full blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not a heart attack, but still serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s why we’re taking it seriously. We’ve scheduled a cardiac catheterization for tomorrow to look at your arteries."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will they fix it if there’s a blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if they find a significant narrowing, they can place another stent. Given your history, it’s possible there’s restenosis — that’s when a stent narrows again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that word from last time. How risky is the procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s generally safe. You’ll be awake but sedated. The team will go through your wrist or groin. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust them. And my knee — I fell a few days ago and hurt my right knee. They put a brace on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the X-ray showed a minimally displaced patella fracture. It’s not bad enough for surgery. We’ll manage it with the brace and follow up with orthopedics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2181-01-11 02:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good, because I don’t want another surgery. My left knee’s already braced from arthritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Mr. ___ , good news. The cath is done. They found a 90% blockage in the distal part of your right coronary artery, right where your old stents are."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So they put in another stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, one drug-eluting stent was placed successfully. No residual narrowing. Your blood flow is restored."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Does that mean the chest pain should stop?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ll keep you on aspirin and Plavix to prevent clots from forming in the stent. You’ll need to stay on those long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m already on them. Any other changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue your atorvastatin, metoprolol, and other home meds. Your labs are stable. Your kidney function improved slightly after dialysis yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had dialysis yesterday? I didn’t know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we scheduled it while you were in the cath lab. Your creatinine dropped from 6.4 to 5.2, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. My potassium was high last time — is it okay now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was 6.7 this morning, which is a bit high, but we’re monitoring it. We’ll adjust your diet and meds before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I need to be careful with that. Any other tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2181-01-11 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an ultrasound of your leg to check for blood clots — all clear. And your chest X-ray shows an enlarged heart, which we already knew about, but no pneumonia or fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your heart meds — aspirin, Plavix, atorvastatin, metoprolol. Avoid heavy lifting and saturated fats — no red meat or cheese. Follow up with your cardiologist and PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my knee?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the brace on, avoid putting full weight on it. See orthopedics next week. We’ve added docusate and senna for constipation — common with pain meds and inactivity."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. And dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back to your regular schedule. Weigh yourself every morning. Call if you gain more than three pounds — could mean fluid buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep track. Thank you, doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You handled everything well. We’ll have your son pick you up soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, he’s on his way. Thanks again for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2181-01-12 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Our pleasure. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if anything changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2181-01-11 02:04:00",
    "admission_end": "2181-01-12 18:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis and a history of multiple coronary stents was admitted for evaluation of recurrent chest pain. The pain, occurring at rest and relieved by nitroglycerin, was consistent with unstable angina. Cardiac catheterization revealed a 90% stenosis in the distal right coronary artery, where a drug-eluting stent was successfully placed. The patient tolerated the procedure well, with resolution of symptoms. He also had a minimally displaced right patellar fracture from a recent fall, managed non-operatively with bracing. He received dialysis during admission, and his medications were continued without complications. He was discharged home with instructions to follow up with cardiology, primary care, and orthopedics, and to maintain a heart-healthy diet and daily weight monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Atherosclerotic heart disease of native coronary artery with unstable angina pectoris",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Dependence on renal dialysis",
      "Other fracture of right patella, initial encounter for closed fracture",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified asthma, uncomplicated",
      "Presence of coronary angioplasty implant and graft",
      "Anemia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
